flow "Quorum reads and writes (R + W > N)"
summary "Overlapping read and write quorums guarantee reading the latest version, while R + W <= N allows stale reads."
tags quorum replication consistency
level intermediate
source "https://www.allthingsdistributed.com/files/amazon-dynamo-sosp2007.pdf"
related distributed-systems/hinted-handoff distributed-systems/read-repair

node client "Client" actor
node coord "Coordinator" service tone=primary
group replicas "Replicas (N=3)"
node r1 "Replica 1" db in=replicas
node r2 "Replica 2" db in=replicas
node r3 "Replica 3" db in=replicas
edge client > coord
edge coord > r1
edge coord > r2
edge coord > r3
array vals "Stored value@ver" keys=r1,r2,r3 = v1@1 v1@1 v1@1

scenario quorum-rw "Strict quorum (W=2, R=2, N=3)"
  step write-w2 "Write succeeds after W=2 replicas ack"
    "Client writes `v2@2`. The coordinator sends it to all 3 replicas; R1 and R2 persist it while R3 is slow. Because `W=2` acks arrived, the write succeeds immediately."
    detail "In Dynamo's quorum protocol, write latency is dictated by the slowest of the `W` responding replicas and read latency by the slowest of `R`. Setting `R` and `W` strictly less than `N` (commonly `N=3, R=2, W=2`) avoids waiting on the single slowest replica."
    send client > coord "PUT v2@2"
    state coord active
    send coord > r1 "v2@2"
    send coord > r2 "v2@2" with
    label vals#r1 "v2@2"
    label vals#r2 "v2@2" with
    state r1,r2,vals#r1,vals#r2 success with
    state r3 warning
    send coord > client "OK (W=2)"
  step read-r2 "Read queries R=2 replicas (R2 and R3)"
    "Next, a client reads with `R=2`. Because `R + W = 4 > 3`, **any** 2 replicas must overlap with the write quorum — here R2 has `v2@2` while R3 still has `v1@1`."
    send client > coord "GET k"
    send coord > r2 "GET"
    send coord > r3 "GET" with
    send r2 > coord "v2@2"
    send r3 > coord "v1@1" with
  step pick-latest "Higher version wins: return v2@2"
    "The coordinator compares versions (`2 > 1`), returns fresh `v2@2` to the client, and can repair R3 in the background."
    detail "When a write descends directly from an earlier version, Dynamo overwrites the older copy automatically. When concurrent writers create causally unrelated versions (incomparable vector clocks), the coordinator returns all divergent versions so the application can reconcile them and write the merged value back."
    send coord > client "v2@2"
    state coord success
    focus r1,r2,r3 dim
    callout coord "R+W > N forces quorum overlap"

scenario stale-read "Stale read when R + W <= N (W=2, R=1)" from=quorum-rw/write-w2
  step weak-read "Read asks only R=1 replica (R3)"
    "To cut read latency, the app lowers `R` to `1`. Now `R + W = 3 <= N`, so the read set no longer has to intersect the write quorum."
    send client > coord "GET k (R=1)"
    send coord > r3 "GET"
    send r3 > coord "v1@1"
  step stale-reply "Client receives stale v1@1"
    "R3 missed the write and returns `v1@1`. Tuning `R` and `W` lets you trade latency and availability against freshness."
    state r3 error
    effect r3 shake
    send coord > client "v1@1 (STALE)"
    state vals#r3 error with
    callout r3 "Missed write quorum: R+W <= N"
